I am writing to register an urgent appeal against a wrongful penalty deduction of \u20B9${deductionAmount} levied on my partner account for Order/Trip Ref: #${orderOrTicketId}.

Incident Summary:
${incidentDescription}

Grounds of Appeal:
1. Force Majeure & Environmental Obstacles: The recorded transit duration was influenced by documented heavy rainfall and waterlogging in the sector, not rider negligence.
2. Good Faith Fulfilment: The delivery was successfully handed over with direct confirmation from the customer doorstep.
3. Lack of Human Review: The penalty was executed algorithmically without providing me an opportunity to explain or submit route telemetry.

In accordance with fair partnership guidelines and statutory gig worker welfare norms, I request an immediate reversal and credit of \u20B9${deductionAmount} to my linked bank account within 48 hours.

Sincerely,
${workerName}
Registered Contact: ${workerPhone}`
        },
        laborCommissionerPetition: {
          title: `FORMAL GRIEVANCE PETITION UNDER GIG & UNORGANIZED WORKERS WELFARE GUIDELINES`,
          body: `BEFORE THE DISTRICT LABOR OFFICER & GIG WORKERS WELFARE TRIBUNAL

In the Matter of: ${workerName} (Complainant)
Versus
${platformName} (Respondent Aggregator)

COMPLAINT UNDER SECTION 7 (UNLAWFUL DEDUCTIONS) & SOCIAL SECURITY CODE

1. The Complainant is a registered platform worker providing frontline delivery/transit services through Respondent's digital application.
2. On the date in question (Ref #${orderOrTicketId}), Respondent unilaterally withheld an amount of \u20B9${deductionAmount} from Complainant's weekly payout without due process or show-cause inquiry.
